A||||7||86SE||EGR valve??||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||01-12-2000||06:22 PM||||My engine throws off a code 32 (EGR valve) the service engine light comes on when the engine reaches 180-200 degrees, can an EGR error damage an engine/damper performance??||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||01-12-2000||07:48 PM||||Yes, a non-functional EGR valve will damage your engine through elevated combustion temperatures, which causes detonation and eventually burnt pistons. I've seen pistons with holes burnt through the ring lands because of detonation. You may not pass emissions because your NOX emissions will be elevated also. <P>EGR Valves do cause you to LOSE some power, but only at part throttle situations. At full throttle the EGR valve is disabled by the computer and therefore does not hurt performance. EGR is an acronym for Exhaust Gas Recirculation and cools the combustion gases buy introducing an inert gas (exhaust gass) along with the mixture.<P>It is not worth disabling the EGR valve to gain some kind of performance gain, It hardly makes a difference. Some guys do this and put higher-octane fuel in their tanks to ward off detonation. They think it makes a huge difference. I call this psychological horsepower, it only exist in their heads.  <P>To see if your EGR valve is working apply vacuum to the valve with the engine idling. If the engine stalls it’s NOT the valve. Make sure that the valve holds a vacuum also. <P>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-12-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||01-12-2000||08:12 PM||||What 88formula said... <P>Also... On a V6 the EGR valve is operated by a solenoid. Code 32 is set when a diagnostic switch either sees vacuum when it shouldn't (bad solenoid or bad wiring) or doesn't see vacuum when it should (leaking vacuum lines, bad wiring, bad solenoid or bad EGR). The link below has a diagram and futher explanation. Bottom line is that code 32 does not neccessarily mean the EGR valve itself is bad.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/EGR-solenoid.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/EGR-solenoid.html</A> <P>BTW, this is NOT something that is damaging like "pull it over and have it towed". It is something that should be fixed but you can drive it in the meantime. Might want to run Premium gas until it is fixed. And listen for pinging (detonation)... if it does then change gears, let off gas, whatever to make it stop... pinging is bad on pistons!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||AL||01-12-2000||08:18 PM||||YOU CAN TAKE THE SOLENOID OFF AND TAKE IT APART CAREFULLY AND CLEAN THE INSIDE AND THE TUBES, that's what i did and the code is gone.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||01-13-2000||08:31 AM||||I was about to start a new post this morning but 86SE beat me to it.  <P>I had the same thing happen to me the last 2 days.  Light comes on after about 5 min and stays on.  Code 32.  <P>The Haynes manual says to check the EGR system......disconnect the solenoid vacuum harness?  Rotate it?? and reinstall only the EGR valve side???  What are they talking about.  They also mention a diagnostic terminal and EGR filter???<P>I can just replace everything but the solenoid is around $80 and the valve is about $40 from the Fiero store.  Thats $120 and may not even be the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||01-14-2000||02:47 PM||||I used to get the code 32 only after 5 minutes or so of highway driving.  I don't get any codes now since my engine is out, but while dismantling it yesterday, I found that a chunk of the gasket between the EGR valve and the crossover pipe was gone, probably creating a vacuum leak when the valve was <BR>activated.  I am hoping this was the source of the code 32, but won't know until my engine is finished in a month or so.||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||01-14-2000||10:36 PM||||If I run the engine for about 10 min of so to get it up to temp, i can reach my fingers up in the EGR valve to give it vacume and the engine just barely stumbles, but does not come close to stalling, is this a sign of a bad EGR valve and just the valve??||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fieroguy1||01-14-2000||10:57 PM||||Mshill, code 32 is lack of vacuum at the egr <BR>solenoid or no signal at same to the eec. So <BR>check your connections. I,had the same problem when the elect. connector came loose while driving. ||||reg||4
